<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders to buy Oct gasoline and naphtha.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders to buy Oct gasoline and naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) had issued two tenders for the purchase of gasoline and naptha, a company offical said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender for the purchase of gasoline calls for the delivery of 250,000 barrels of 95-octane unleaded grade during September 16-30. The tender closes on September 3 and would be valid for two days.</p>
<p>CPC's tender for the purchase of naphtha requires the delivery of 30,000 tonnes during September 21-31. The tender closes on September 2.</p>
<p>Both cargoes are to be delivered to Keelung or Taichung on a cost-and-freight basis.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-870-3093)</p>
